Retrolarium Studio {version}

Edit levels, graphics, palettes, text, music, sound effects and demos, then
play the result in MAME. Windows 10/11, 64-bit. The ZIP runs after unpacking;
the installer installs for your user without administrator rights.

Supported games: Super Mario Bros. and supported FDS/Vs. variants, Pac-Man,
Castle Excellent/Castlequest, Doraemon, Solomon's Key, Flicky and Alien Soldier.
Use your own ROM. No game ROMs or original console BIOS dumps are supplied.
Internet is needed when a game's source repository is first downloaded.
Only the exact revisions in the Kit catalog are recognized automatically.

The application is unsigned. Windows/SmartScreen or local security policy
may show a warning or block it. Check SHA256SUMS.txt from the download first.

Your games, ROM copies and edits normally live in Documents/Retrolarium.
Saves and movies also use %LOCALAPPDATA%/Retrolarium/Retrolarium Studio.
Verification records live in %LOCALAPPDATA%/Retrolarium/Kit/verified; a record
inside a downloaded project never grants trust. Before running a verified
repository's scripts, Studio asks for consent for its pinned content digest.

User guide: {studio_file_url}/docs/user_guide.md
Supported ROM revisions and SHA-256: {kit_file_url}/docs/supported_roms.md
Build instructions: {studio_file_url}/docs/developing.md

Exact corresponding sources for this package:
Studio: {studio_url}
Kit (Python sources are also in kit/): {kit_url}
Core (Python sources are also in kit/): {core_url}
Longreach Qt SDK recipes and Qt patches: {longreach_url}
Qt {qt_version} complete source archive: {qt_source_url}
Qt source archive SHA-256: {qt_source_sha256}
MAME: {mame_url}
MAME build recipe: {studio_file_url}/tools/build-mame-docker.ps1
Python {python_version}: {python_url}
OpenDiskSysROM: {bios_url}

BUILD-INFO.txt and native-build.json record the exact commits, build inputs
and binary hashes. This is identified by source commits; new release tags
are chosen separately and are not assumed from the displayed version.

Studio is GPL-3.0-or-later; see LICENSE.txt. Qt is linked statically. The
complete Studio/Core sources and SDK recipe above allow rebuilding with
a modified Qt. See THIRD-PARTY.txt, licenses/, mame/COPYING, mame/legal/,
python/LICENSE.txt and the Kit component folders for license notices.
The original LGPL OpenDiskSysROM is used for FDS games; it is not Nintendo's BIOS.

Game titles and characters are trademarks of their respective owners.
